  "proved_structural_results": [
    "For the original beta(4) matrix E=q+beta(4)I, an explicit all-prime and all-prime-power integer Ghat_n satisfies Ghat_n det(q+TI) in Z[T], with log Ghat_n <= (771/40)n^2+o(n^2). This is an upper bound on the paid integral-model cost, not an optimality claim.",
    "The actual full column pool obeys det[C|L]=delta_n det E, with delta_n a nonzero exact confluent Cauchy determinant; its local valuations are explicit. This proves constraint normality, not period-pairing nonvanishing.",
    "Actual projected rows have forced Mellin sign changes, and explicit n=2 positive-interval and negative-axis evaluation counterexamples. These exclude the stated direct AT/Chebyshev shortcuts, not the actual integrated determinant.",
    "For n=p>=13 the true projection is p-integral, its extra rows are p-divisible and matching extra rows are p^2-divisible. Paid p^3/p^4 column scalings give a low skew-Cauchy block and a unit high diagonal block.",
    "For the single finite scale n=p=23 and every T in Z_23, det(q+TI_23) is nonzero with valuation -86, by the p-unit Pfaffian 2593/2160. Applied to a rational beta(4), this requires that its reduced denominator be coprime to 23; no unknown real period is directly specialized into Q_23."
  ],
  "important_limitations": [
    "The 771/40 fee is only the safe all-prime integral-model upper rate. The nonzero integer lower bound additionally assumes a rational target with its fixed denominator paid and actual determinant nonvanishing.",
    "A finite n=23 certificate is not infinitely many scales, does not establish n=23^j nonvanishing, and does not exclude rational targets with denominator divisible by 23.",
    "The p=13 leading-layer failure and the odd-dimensional skew-block failures do not prove the actual determinant vanishes.",
    "Constraint regularity, monicity and raw positive kernels do not imply the projected determinant is nonzero.",
    "Paper reviews, physical hashes and repository synchronization are not Lean formal verification."
  ],
  "remaining_gaps": [
    "Infinite-scale nonvanishing of the same actual projected single-beta determinant.",
    "Sufficient real-place decay of that same E determinant to beat the paid 771/40 rate and produce a strict analytic-arithmetic margin.",
    "A paid transfer of the finite p=23 block structure to growing prime-power scales, including new denominator layers, Taylor jets and Frobenius/carry changes."
  ],
